{
  "kind": "floret.patch",
  "version": 4,
  "appVersion": "0.0.1",
  "meta": {
    "name": "Orbital Sandbox",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "orb_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -364
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Orbital sandbox\n\nBodies orbit a pair of stars that circle each other, so no orbit quite repeats: a three-body system you can play with. Every frame each body's velocity takes the pull of both stars (the Gravity subpatch: stronger the closer it is, softened right next to a star) and its position takes the new velocity (Move) — positions and velocities live in Read* / Write* state. Bodies that fall into a star or fly off are dropped.\n\n• Drag on the canvas and let go to launch a body: it flies from where you pressed, away from the cursor, faster the longer the pull.\n• Slider into `warp`: time warp (0.25× – 3×).\n• Slider into `sep`: the stars' separation (small = one star, steady Kepler orbits; wide = chaos).\n• Toggle: orbit trails (Echo).",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Orbital sandbox\n\nBodies orbit a pair of stars that circle each other, so no orbit quite repeats: a three-body system you can play with. Every frame each body's velocity takes the pull of both stars (the Gravity subpatch: stronger the closer it is, softened right next to a star) and its position takes the new velocity (Move) — positions and velocities live in Read* / Write* state. Bodies that fall into a star or fly off are dropped.\n\n• Drag on the canvas and let go to launch a body: it flies from where you pressed, away from the cursor, faster the longer the pull.\n• Slider into `warp`: time warp (0.25× – 3×).\n• Slider into `sep`: the stars' separation (small = one star, steady Kepler orbits; wide = chaos).\n• Toggle: orbit trails (Echo).",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
